adr: 0227
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: constexpr_errors
why: D.9 makes ln of a value that is *not positive* an error, so zero is inside the error and not on its edge. Testing for a negative value alone leaves ln(0.0) to the call, which traps -- and the boundary is exactly where a reading of the clause can go wrong without any other case noticing.
--- old
              if x <= 0.0 then begin
--- new
              if x < 0.0 then begin
